<h2 id="why-philly">Why Philly is a good city for side income</h2>
<p>Philadelphia packs a lot of demand into a small footprint. A delivery driver in Center City can finish three orders in the time it takes to finish one in a sprawling Sun Belt suburb, and a dog walker in Fishtown can stack five clients on two blocks.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Eds and meds.</strong> Penn, Drexel, Temple, Jefferson, Saint Joseph's and La Salle bring tens of thousands of students, while Penn Medicine, CHOP, Jefferson Health and Temple Health employ huge, shift-working staffs who outsource errands, pet care and cleaning.</li>
  <li><strong>The South Philly sports complex.</strong> Eagles games at Lincoln Financial Field, Phillies at Citizens Bank Park, and Sixers and Flyers at the Wells Fargo Center create predictable rideshare, parking and staffing surges.</li>
  <li><strong>A year-round event calendar.</strong> The Mummers Parade on New Year's Day, the Flower Show in late winter, the Penn Relays and Broad Street Run in spring, Wawa Welcome America around July 4 and the Philadelphia Marathon in November all bring crowds.</li>
